# Portfolio Section Navigation

## How users move

- **Desktop:** ArrowUp / ArrowDown (also PageUp / PageDown). Wheel / touch show a hint only.
- **Mobile (≤860px):** swipe / wheel advances sections — no keyboard required.
- Secondary: section slider + in-content `goTo` / `jumpTo` buttons.
- Nested card scroll still works with touch/wheel until the card hits its edge; then section nav takes over.

## Ownership

- Section index + ↑/↓ key handling live at **App root** (`App.jsx` + `useSectionNav`).
- ❌ Do not attach ArrowUp/ArrowDown handlers inside section cards or scroll areas.
- ❌ Do not let nested scroll containers consume ↑/↓ for scrolling.
- ✅ Horizontal ←/→ may still drive the projects carousel only.

## Arrow key contract

When ↑/↓ (or PageUp/PageDown) is pressed anywhere on the site:

1. `preventDefault` + `stopImmediatePropagation` in the **capture** phase.
2. Advance / retreat one section — **cursor position does not matter**.
3. Scrollable cards (`.thin-scroll`, `.no-scrollbar`) must **never** scroll from ↑/↓.
4. Only exception: focused `INPUT` / `TEXTAREA` / `SELECT` / `contentEditable` (caret / value editing).
5. When `body.nav-paused` (e.g. project modal), skip section changes.

## When editing cards

- Wheel/touch may still scroll card interiors.
- Never rely on default browser arrow-key scrolling inside panels.
- Keep Escape-to-close (and similar) local; do not steal ↑/↓.
